<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hachisuka Yoshishige</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1586–<a href="/years/1620">1620</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hachisuka Yoshishige was the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/daimyo">daimyo</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokushima">Tokushima</a> domain on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shikoku">Shikoku</a>. The son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hachisuka-iemasa">Hachisuka Iemasa</a>, he fought for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-ieyasu">Tokugawa Ieyasu</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-sekigahara">Sekigahara</a> campaign of 1600 while his father withdrew from public life, and was confirmed in Awa province. For his service in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osaka">Osaka</a> campaigns the island of Awaji was added to his domain in 1615, raising it to about 257,000 koku.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hachisuka-yoshishige.jpg" alt="Hachisuka Yoshishige" width="320" height="578" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hachisuka_Yoshishige.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
